 <iati-activity default-currency="EUR" hierarchy="2" humanitarian="0" iati-activities:version="2.02" xml:lang="EN" xmlns:iati-activities="http://d-portal.org/xmlns/iati-activities" xmlns:xsd="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema" xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance">
  <iati-identifier>NL-KVK-40409352-PRJ13-219-0108</iati-identifier>
  <reporting-org ref="NL-KVK-40409352" type="21">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Netherlands Red Cross</narrative>
  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Sudan Localization project (2024 - 2026)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Port Sudan, Sudan, with impact country-wide.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="3">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Sudanese Red Crescent Society (SRCS)</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The ongoing conflict in Sudan has huge negative impact on SRCS operations, restricting access to its former HQ and facing destruction of essential infrastructure due to the ongoing hostilities. SRCS is being supported by its partners to keep the business continued. In November 2023, a business continuity plan was developed and shared with partners for support. In August 2024, the national society, with support from its partners, has developed an NSD plan for 2025 to 2030. This project supports some of the key priorities of this plan.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The support will focus on supporting
- the further development of capacities in data and information management for humanitarian service delivery
- training on and learning and mainstreaming of CEA 
- the organization in becoming a more financially sustainable organisation
- technical functions of SRCS as prioritized in their strategy</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project aims to sustain and improve the current capacity of Sudanese Red Crescent Society (SRCS) to provide assistance to the affected population of Sudan in the current context of conflict and set up the long-term basis for its effective recovery and development. Specific focus areas include Financial Sustainablity (FS), Data and Digitalisation (D&amp;D) and Community Engagement and Accountability (CEA).</narrative>
  </description>
